  "notes": "ちょっと is a versatile word used to soften statements, express small amounts, or get attention.\n\nKEY USES:\n1. A little/slightly: ちょっと{高|たか}い (a bit expensive)\n2. Brief time: ちょっと{待|ま}って (wait a moment)\n3. Softener: ちょっと{いい}ですか (excuse me, do you have a moment?)\n4. Polite refusal: ちょっと... (implies \"that's difficult\")\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- ちょっとした〜: a small ~, a minor ~\n- ちょっとしたことで: over a trivial matter\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n{少|すこ}し: a little (slightly more formal, precise)",
